Cell["\<\
reciprocalBasis contains reciprocal basis vectors as rows and must be an \
exact 2 by 2 or 3 by 3 matrix; the implementation requires \
Precision[reciprocalBasis] == Infinity.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->961843519,ExpressionUUID->"447e9997-39a1-834b-891b-6ebb7bcbba30"],

Cell["\<\
n defaults to 2. Lattice points with each integer coefficient between -n and \
n are used to construct a Voronoi mesh.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1630276497,ExpressionUUID->"8293cbf2-0f94-9540-ad4b-b810cf3c30b9"],

Cell["\<\
Returns the full-dimensional mesh primitive whose centroid lies within 10^-5 \
of the origin. For strongly skewed bases, increase n and check that the zone \
has converged.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1226921726,ExpressionUUID->"0a4476d3-d271-3547-8677-c4849049e232"]
}, Closed]],

